 choose to play  anyhow like i said the game is free so  if you want to support my channel then  be sure to download this like today  using the link in the description and  you can also use my code to get special  rewards  okay so to explain this armature in  theory we need to flash back around 2000  years to a time when there was only one  shifter on the entire planet that  shifter was of course the original  founding titan ymir and after her death  king fritz was desperate to make sure  that the elding empire didn't lose her  power  since she was the first ever titan  nobody knew if her abilities could be  passed down and so he made his daughters  eat emir in the hope that maybe that  would do something luckily for fritz the  idea worked even better than he could  have hoped as emir's power wasn't just  passed down to one person but rather it  was divided between the three of them  mario rosenstein each inherited their  own unique time shifters that had never  been seen before and in the process they  became the first hybrid titans what i  mean by hybrids is that their three  shifters would have had a mixture of  different traits from emir for instance  one of them might have been larger than  the others and other might have  specialized in hardening while another  might have had a more beast-like  appearance in a second we'll break down  how them being hybrids is very relevant  to this theory but first let's establish  why ymir's power was split in the first  place  as an audience we're not really used to  the idea of titan powers being divided  like this since most of the time one  person will inherit one shifter and  that's usually the end of it however in  chapter 122 isayama spelled out for us  why yemi's power split into three and  it's all down to the method that fritz  used as we can see when multiple lg's  eat the spine of a shifter at the same  time the powers of that shifter are  divided between all the people consuming  it this is directly proven by what mario  rosencena did because up until this  point we had never seen a group of  people eat the spine simultaneously what  this all means is that fritz discovered  a way for ld to increase the amount of  shifters they had which is why within  just a few generations the empire went  from having only one titan to having an  army of nine these nine titans each had  their own unique characteristics as we  know but from the beginning it was  obvious that some were more closely  related than others for example the draw  card and beast titans all share  animalistic features that none of the  other shifters possess and in the final  arc of the series iseyama went out of  his way to highlight just how similar  they are the blatant resemblance between  them isn't a coincidence but rather it's  the result of these three titans  descending from the same titan hybrid in  that way the beast carton draw would  essentially be siblings as the three of  them descended from one specific  daughter of emir the same is true when  we examine the attack female and  colossal who each have an interesting  connection it goes without saying that  the relation between the female and  attack titan is easy to explain as they  pretty much have the exact same athletic  physique this physique allows them to  have decent levels of stamina with aaron  displaying that during the raid on  liberio and annie displaying it in the  manga when the warriors first arrived  when it comes to the colossal though its  massive size and lack of stamina is  drastically different from the other two  but what it does have is a body lacking  skin which is a unique trait to both  this and the female titan  finally this brings us to the last and  for this video the most important trio  of titans which are the armor warhammer  and founder when we look into their  history it's undeniable that these three  are the most naturally gifted when it  comes to harnessing the power of titan  hardening for two thousand years they've  evidenced this in various ways whether  it be culprits using the founder to form  the three enormous walls on parodies or  whether it's the warhammer using this  power to create any weapon they want  we've already established that the nine  times of today are simply offshoots of  hybrid titans that used to exist so it  stands to reason that 2000 years ago the  first armored titan was a hybrid between  the armor and warhammer this is  supported by the fact that when you  examine them side by side they're the  only shifters in history to ever have  some kind of shell or plates built onto  their body that alone makes it clear  that they are closely related in much  the same way as the draw on card titan  and it's where the idea for this theory  came from to put it simply what this  video is proposing is that after the  daughter of emir died her shift was  split between two children one who  gained the power of the founding titan  and another who inherited something that  had never been seen before this hybrid  shifter would have been a primitive  version of what we now call the armor  titan but at the time its physical  appearance would have been entirely new  i imagine the hardening surrounding its  body would be significantly thicker than  in the present day which would limit the  mobility of this titan and make its  movement slow compared to the others the  reason this would be the case is because  this time would be like a prototype for  yamir as it would be her first time  sculpting a titan like this in the past  dimension  it's kind of implied that she's mostly  responsible for the design of each titan  and given that this would be her first  shifter with built-in armor there's  bound to be something about it that  would be a little bit unrefined however  one benefit of the thick armor is that  it would be quite literally unbreakable  especially when you consider that back  then no army would have anything close  to armor-piercing bullets  on top of that this 